        "original_id": "ba0eecaa-2eed-5903-bef1-e262cabb522e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: South London, England, south-east England, Central London, Crawley\n- Products: Croydon Airport, Northolt Aerodrome, London Heathrow Airport, Gatwick Airport\n- Concepts: airport codes, airport status, airport importance\n\nFacts:\n- Croydon Airport had the ICAO code EGCR and was an airport in South London, England.\n- Croydon Airport was the main airport for London before Northolt Aerodrome, London Heathrow Airport, and Gatwick Airport replaced it.\n- Gatwick Airport, also known as London Gatwick, has the IATA code LGW and the ICAO code EGKK.\n- Gatwick Airport is a major international airport in south-east England, 29.5 miles south of Central London and 2.7 nautical miles north of Crawley.\n- Gatwick Airport is the eighth-busiest airport in Europe.",
